      "id": "ISA.25.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.25.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall be said in that day, Lo, this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our God; we have waited for him, and he will save us: this is the LORD, we have waited for him, we will be glad and rejoice in his salvation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.25.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.25.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For on this mountain shall the hand of the LORD rest, and Moab shall be trodden down under him, even as straw is trodden down for the dunghill.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.25.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.25.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will spread forth his hands in the midst of them, as he that swimmeth spreadeth forth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his hands",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to swim: and he will bring down their pride together with the spoils of their hands.",
